\chapter{The CloudXRKit Backend}\label{ch:classic}

The classic backend is NVIDIA's original code path. This chapter adapts its session to
[[ViewerSession]] and then presents the configuration form's logic, which connects either backend.

\section{The adapter}

[[ClassicSession]] wraps a CloudXRKit [[Session]]. It stores nothing but the session, so it can be
created on demand (Section~\ref{sec:active}). The status mapping is a direct translation; the
[[@unknown default]] is required because CloudXRKit is built with library evolution and may add
states in a later version.

<<CloudXRViewer/Common/Streaming/ClassicSession.swift>>=
<<MIT permission notice>>
// Copyright (c) 2026 Pablo Figueroa and Claude.

import CloudXRKit
import Foundation

/// Adapts a CloudXRKit `Session` to `ViewerSession`.
///
/// The adapter keeps no state of its own: every property reads through to the wrapped session, so
/// SwiftUI observation of `Session.state` keeps working through it.
@MainActor
final class ClassicSession: ViewerSession {
    let session: Session

    init(_ session: Session) {
        self.session = session
    }

    var viewerStatus: ViewerStatus {
        switch session.state {
        case .initialized:
            .initialized
        case .authenticating, .authenticated, .connecting:
            .connecting
        case .connected:
            .connected
        case .pausing:
            .pausing
        case .paused:
            .paused
        case .resuming:
            .resuming
        case .disconnecting:
            .disconnecting
        case .disconnected(let result):
            switch result {
            case .success:
                .disconnected(error: nil)
            case .failure(let error):
                .disconnected(error: error.localizedDescription)
            }
        @unknown default:
            .initialized
        }
    }

@
CloudXRKit names a channel by a [[ChannelInfo]] whose [[uuid]] is a byte array; the label
prints those bytes as NVIDIA's picker did.

<<CloudXRViewer/Common/Streaming/ClassicSession.swift>>=
    var statusDescription: String {
        session.state.description
    }

    var channelIDs: [ViewerChannelID] {
        session.availableMessageChannels.map { channelInfo in
            ViewerChannelID(
                label: "Channel [\(channelInfo.uuid.map { String($0) }.joined(separator: ","))]",
                key: channelInfo
            )
        }
    }

    func channel(for id: ViewerChannelID) -> (any ViewerChannel)? {
        guard let channelInfo = id.key.base as? ChannelInfo else {
            return nil
        }
        return session.getMessageChannel(channelInfo)
    }

@
The lifecycle calls forward to CloudXRKit's synchronous versions.

<<CloudXRViewer/Common/Streaming/ClassicSession.swift>>=
    func disconnect() async {
        session.disconnect()
    }

    func pause() async throws {
        session.pause()
    }

    func resume() async throws {
        try session.resume()
    }
}

@
CloudXRKit's channel class conforms to [[ViewerChannel]] through an extension, so no
wrapper object is needed.

<<CloudXRViewer/Common/Streaming/ClassicSession.swift>>=
extension CloudXRKit.MessageChannel: ViewerChannel {
    var statusDescription: String {
        status.rawValue
    }

    func send(_ data: Data) throws {
        guard sendServerMessage(data) else {
            throw ChannelSendError()
        }
    }
}
